  "changes": [
    "OSC caches padded addresses and type tags; bulk integer truncation, normalization and big-endian float32 encoding replace per-message builder/reparse. Packet count, arrays, destination and duplicate suppression unchanged.",
    "E1.31 precomputes channel intersections and converts each input frame once. The public sACN setter still validates bytes and marks output changes; synchronization and sender lifecycle retained.",
    "E1.31 whole-universe channel offsets previously crashed (8 failing parameterized tests before fix); intersections now correctly skip untouched universes."
  ],
  "remaining_hotspots": [
    "E1.31 encoding: 53.24% validation generator plus 23.90% setter in sACN DataPacket.dmxData; LedFx flush self share falls from 46.38% to 11.93%.",
    "OSC loopback: 95.56% of samples in benchmark Sink.send (socket send plus accounting). Per-address datagram count now dominates; reducing it requires receiver/protocol compatibility work."
  ],
